 ],
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "There's a creek between your house and the road, so you decide to build a bridge. Easy, right?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "You drop a big tree trunk across it. It works, but it's slippery and only one person wide.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you nail wooden planks on top and add a handrail. Now a cart can cross.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But wood that stays wet starts to rot. After a few years, the planks turn soft and green.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "One day a loaded cart rolls over the middle, and the whole bridge sags.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The problem is the span: thirteen meters of wood with nothing holding up the middle.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pour a concrete pier in the middle of the creek. Two short spans are much stronger.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then the spring storm comes. The creek rises almost three meters in one night.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Branches pile up against the pier, the water pushes, and your bridge is carried away.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So this time you build a stone arch, high above the water, with nothing standing in the creek.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every stone pushes on the next one, and the weight flows down into the banks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But stone arches are slow and expensive to build. Today, you'd use a steel truss.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Triangles can't bend out of shape, so a light frame can carry heavy trucks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And its bottom sits well above the highest flood anyone has ever recorded.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just bridged the creek for good. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
